 "text": "You don't need a free week for a big goal, you need three half hours. Even a packed week has them, before work a lunch break Sunday morning, but finding them is the easy part. Say the goal is your first podcast episode, tonight put three 30-minute blocks in your calendar. Then give each block one output, not a topic. Monday outline episode one, Wednesday record a 10-minute test, Sunday listen back and fix one thing. That's 90 minutes and by Sunday the episode exists. Send this to the friend who's waiting for a quiet month. That's what Demure is for, you archive your dream today so you can see it tomorrow and break it down into small steps you can actually do. Follow for one fix a day, this afternoon the phone habit you don't notice. If you want to try it out I've put the link in the bio.",
